source: crates/togi/tests/cli/mod.rs
expression: "help(\"reset\")"
---
Archive the whole session

Archive the whole session, so the next run starts a new one. The reset is a permanent boundary: the new session imports no record from the archived session or anything before it.

--all archives a journal of any ruleset, schema or evidence epoch, but on a journal of the same schema refuses an unknown event kind or field; install the build that wrote them. Only one run or reset can own this machine, even with different state directories. A busy host lock stops reset before it changes the session.

Usage: togi reset [OPTIONS] --all

Options:
      --all
          Archive the session; the next run starts a new one

      --state-dir <path>
          State directory
          
          [default: /var/lib/togi]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Examples:
  sudo togi reset --all   Archive the session and start over
